  "problem": "The marginal mass functions of the independent discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ are shown below. Given that the corresponding joint probability mass function is $f(x,y),$ find $f(2,5).$\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">${f}_{X}(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"50\"></th>\n<th>\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">${f}_{Y}(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.5$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th></tr></tbody></table>",
